(4747679, 684798, 33096, '<td valign="top">Good shot, the setting is impressive and the colour variation in the stars wis very good.  Perhaps keeping the shutter open a bit longer would have improved the look by curving the stars more.</td>', 'Good shot, the setting is impressive and the colour variation in the stars wis very good.  Perhaps keeping the shutter open a bit longer would have improved the look by curving the stars more.', '2008-06-04 09:08:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(4747684, 684061, 90495, '<td valign="top"><strike>Crappy title but great exposure.</strike> <br/> <br/>I take that back. Must have been in a grumpy mood that day. I like the inclusion of the treeline in this shot. But I don''t get it though, if you''re tracking the stars, why aren''t the trees blurry? I presume the software uses one exposure for earth objects and another for the stars.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-08-17 20:33:15.</i></td>', 'Crappy title but great exposure.  I take that back. Must have been in a grumpy mood that day. I like the inclusion of the treeline in this shot. But I don''t get it though, if you''re tracking the stars, why aren''t the trees blurry? I presume the software uses one exposure for earth objects and another for the stars.', '2008-06-04 09:11:00.000000', '2008-08-17 21:33:15.000000', 1),
(4747689, 685479, 33096, '<td valign="top">nice photo, the trees are good, but perhpas having polaris (the northstar) in the shot would have framed it better.  You seem to have plenty of stuck pixles, a darkframe would have helped.</td>', 'nice photo, the trees are good, but perhpas having polaris (the northstar) in the shot would have framed it better.  You seem to have plenty of stuck pixles, a darkframe would have helped.', '2008-06-04 09:12:25.000000', NULL, 1),
