(4761404, 684742, 9462, '<td valign="top">I''m usually not one to be a hard ass about the theme but this one is just too specific to ignore. I absolutely love this photograph , it depicts the late evening/early night sky beautifully, but there''s no moon, stars or planets. I did spot a twinkling something (the plane?) between the arch and the airplane trail, I''ll give you the benefit of the doubt but again this image isn''t <i>heavily </i>dependent on any celestial body. In a monuments challenge you would definitely have yourself a winner.</td>', 'I''m usually not one to be a hard ass about the theme but this one is just too specific to ignore. I absolutely love this photograph , it depicts the late evening/early night sky beautifully, but there''s no moon, stars or planets. I did spot a twinkling something (the plane?) between the arch and the airplane trail, I''ll give you the benefit of the doubt but again this image isn''t heavily dependent on any celestial body. In a monuments challenge you would definitely have yourself a winner.', '2008-06-10 12:31:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761419, 685354, 9462, '<td valign="top">I''m curious if you''re shooting with a Nikon and the 10.5mm... the reason being; those faint purple spots on the right border are reminiscent of what happens to me during night sky exposures longer than 7 minutes. <br/>Easily the best star trail pic of the challenge.<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-11 12:56:16.</i></td>', 'I''m curious if you''re shooting with a Nikon and the 10.5mm... the reason being; those faint purple spots on the right border are reminiscent of what happens to me during night sky exposures longer than 7 minutes. Easily the best star trail pic of the challenge.', '2008-06-10 12:55:28.000000', '2008-06-11 13:56:16.000000', 1),
