(4761639, 685476, 77192, '<td valign="top">Very creative :-)</td>', 'Very creative :-)', '2008-06-10 15:27:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761734, 685475, 811, '<td valign="top">Not a lot here to captivate me, or cause me to think this is a good photograph.  If you want to go with something this "minimal," you could try to add interest by making it look funky in post processing.  As it is, it could be the open sky, or it could be a patch of dryer lint on a window.</td>', 'Not a lot here to captivate me, or cause me to think this is a good photograph.  If you want to go with something this "minimal," you could try to add interest by making it look funky in post processing.  As it is, it could be the open sky, or it could be a patch of dryer lint on a window.', '2008-06-10 16:23:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761745, 685310, 811, '<td valign="top">I like the sharp contrast in this, and the brilliant reds.</td>', 'I like the sharp contrast in this, and the brilliant reds.', '2008-06-10 16:27:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761747, 685384, 811, '<td valign="top">Would be much, much more effective if focus was sharper, I think.  It is just off enough to make it a bit uncomfortable to look at.</td>', 'Would be much, much more effective if focus was sharper, I think.  It is just off enough to make it a bit uncomfortable to look at.', '2008-06-10 16:28:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761748, 685034, 811, '<td valign="top">Did you use a flash?  It is a bit harsh, I think.  Good composition though.</td>', 'Did you use a flash?  It is a bit harsh, I think.  Good composition though.', '2008-06-10 16:28:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761751, 685271, 811, '<td valign="top">Great composition and color tones in this one.  VERY well done.</td>', 'Great composition and color tones in this one.  VERY well done.', '2008-06-10 16:29:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761752, 685125, 811, '<td valign="top">That movies STILL scares me (and it has been well over 20 years since I saw it).  GREAT capture.  Excellent colors and strong composition.</td>', 'That movies STILL scares me (and it has been well over 20 years since I saw it).  GREAT capture.  Excellent colors and strong composition.', '2008-06-10 16:30:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761754, 684061, 811, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done.  I like how it is more concentrated at the bottom of the frame and leads up and to the left.</td>', 'Very nicely done.  I like how it is more concentrated at the bottom of the frame and leads up and to the left.', '2008-06-10 16:30:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761755, 684408, 811, '<td valign="top">That is too cool.  VERY nicely done.</td>', 'That is too cool.  VERY nicely done.', '2008-06-10 16:31:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761769, 685283, 9668, '<td valign="top">Truly amazing how many stars are in the sky. There is a statement by some astronomer at some time that if you point any direction to the night sky, if you follow a direct line from that you will eventually reach a star (even in we can''t see it from earth). For the universe is so expansive, that there is an infinite possibility of that line hitting a star. <br/>I like this, especially that you''ve captured this cluster so well, but I''d rather have the focal point off center.</td>', 'Truly amazing how many stars are in the sky. There is a statement by some astronomer at some time that if you point any direction to the night sky, if you follow a direct line from that you will eventually reach a star (even in we can''t see it from earth). For the universe is so expansive, that there is an infinite possibility of that line hitting a star. I like this, especially that you''ve captured this cluster so well, but I''d rather have the focal point off center.', '2008-06-10 16:41:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761777, 683883, 9668, '<td valign="top">Nice use of slow exposure to blur the lights. Sorry, DNMC to me though - night sky doesn''t cause the impact in this photo. The lights and reflection are cool though. I wonder what this would look like if tilted the camera down another third, so that the line of houses would be up on the upper rule of thirds and you''d see more of that rad reflection.</td>', 'Nice use of slow exposure to blur the lights. Sorry, DNMC to me though - night sky doesn''t cause the impact in this photo. The lights and reflection are cool though. I wonder what this would look like if tilted the camera down another third, so that the line of houses would be up on the upper rule of thirds and you''d see more of that rad reflection.', '2008-06-10 16:44:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761781, 685475, 9668, '<td valign="top">I think DPC may not like this image, but I just love it. It has an awesome feel of an old photograph - with the vignetted edges and the grainy/noisy feel, and even the dust thing (?) in the upper right. It is so simple, but it feels very artistic (which is another thing I don''t think DPC properly appreciates). Awesome image.</td>', 'I think DPC may not like this image, but I just love it. It has an awesome feel of an old photograph - with the vignetted edges and the grainy/noisy feel, and even the dust thing (?) in the upper right. It is so simple, but it feels very artistic (which is another thing I don''t think DPC properly appreciates). Awesome image.', '2008-06-10 16:47:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761784, 685447, 9668, '<td valign="top">Top 10? Great job composing this image with the spiral focused on the upper left rule of third and the mountain along the bottom rule of third. I think this would ribbon if you could see the silhouette of someone standing on top of the left "peak" with their arms outstretched (which would suck to hold for the 1 minute plus time that took you to shoot this =).</td>', 'Top 10? Great job composing this image with the spiral focused on the upper left rule of third and the mountain along the bottom rule of third. I think this would ribbon if you could see the silhouette of someone standing on top of the left "peak" with their arms outstretched (which would suck to hold for the 1 minute plus time that took you to shoot this =).', '2008-06-10 16:50:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761786, 685090, 9668, '<td valign="top">heh! where''d you find this consolation?</td>', 'heh! where''d you find this consolation?', '2008-06-10 16:51:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761788, 683953, 9668, '<td valign="top">Self portrait? for 30 seconds? nicely done.</td>', 'Self portrait? for 30 seconds? nicely done.', '2008-06-10 16:52:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761799, 685354, 9668, '<td valign="top">I''m going to guess this was a 45 minute exposure. I like the trees on the left. I think this may have been a better composition though if you''d cropped of the tree on the right and flipped it vertical.</td>', 'I''m going to guess this was a 45 minute exposure. I like the trees on the left. I think this may have been a better composition though if you''d cropped of the tree on the right and flipped it vertical.', '2008-06-10 17:00:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761800, 685351, 9668, '<td valign="top">Top 10. If not top 3.</td>', 'Top 10. If not top 3.', '2008-06-10 17:01:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761801, 685271, 9668, '<td valign="top">I like the "over-exposure" of this. Great effect.</td>', 'I like the "over-exposure" of this. Great effect.', '2008-06-10 17:01:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761802, 684798, 9668, '<td valign="top">Awesome shot. Love the lines.</td>', 'Awesome shot. Love the lines.', '2008-06-10 17:02:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761804, 685348, 9668, '<td valign="top">Nice capture of star trails.</td>', 'Nice capture of star trails.', '2008-06-10 17:02:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761806, 684408, 9668, '<td valign="top">So rad! Hope this at least gets top 10. I hardly ever see pictures like this on DPC, well done.</td>', 'So rad! Hope this at least gets top 10. I hardly ever see pictures like this on DPC, well done.', '2008-06-10 17:03:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761808, 683783, 9668, '<td valign="top">Nice shot of lightning.</td>', 'Nice shot of lightning.', '2008-06-10 17:04:16.000000', NULL, 1),
