(4761812, 685422, 9668, '<td valign="top">I''m having a hard time believing this is actually a photo of the night sky, because the moon would be so much brighter in comparison to the stars. And the stars doesn''t seem to vary in luminosity like they do in the night sky. That being said, I''m going to vote on this as if a true image.</td>', 'I''m having a hard time believing this is actually a photo of the night sky, because the moon would be so much brighter in comparison to the stars. And the stars doesn''t seem to vary in luminosity like they do in the night sky. That being said, I''m going to vote on this as if a true image.', '2008-06-10 17:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761819, 685314, 9668, '<td valign="top">Reminds me of Monet''s paintings of sunset at the <a href="//www.ibiblio.org/wm/paint/auth/monet/parliament/parliament.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Houses of Parliament </a>. Awesome shot.</td>', 'Reminds me of Monet''s paintings of sunset at the Houses of Parliament . Awesome shot.', '2008-06-10 17:12:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761910, 684061, 54446, '<td valign="top">Beautiful.  Although, the image raises some questions.  If you used an equitorial mount to track the stars and milky way to get this great exposure, why are the trees in unblurred silhouette? edited to add:  Now I understand.  Thank you!  Since your procedure has been validated, this certainly deserves a top score.  (10)</td>', 'Beautiful.  Although, the image raises some questions.  If you used an equitorial mount to track the stars and milky way to get this great exposure, why are the trees in unblurred silhouette? edited to add:  Now I understand.  Thank you!  Since your procedure has been validated, this certainly deserves a top score.  (10)', '2008-06-10 18:08:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(4761915, 684408, 54446, '<td valign="top">Of course, this is beautiful.  Probably the challenge blue ribbon.  There are some hot pixels, which do not look the same as the stars.  The star effect on the shining stars is very nice.  Great astronomy.  Bumping up a bit.</td>', 'Of course, this is beautiful.  Probably the challenge blue ribbon.  There are some hot pixels, which do not look the same as the stars.  The star effect on the shining stars is very nice.  Great astronomy.  Bumping up a bit.', '2008-06-10 18:09:47.000000', NULL, 1),
