(4762885, 685354, 22301, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by benolsen:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>Bvy: no city lights anywhere near, I don''t know where it came from.<br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sorry to hear your shot was before the challenge dates. Its really an amazing shot. :)<br/> I saw you were wondering about the purple on the edge of your image. This is caused from the sensor heating up from being on for so long, it creates little hot spots. It happens with really long exposures. Hope this helps.<br/>Joe<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-11 00:37:18.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by benolsen: Bvy: no city lights anywhere near, I don''t know where it came from.  Sorry to hear your shot was before the challenge dates. Its really an amazing shot. :) I saw you were wondering about the purple on the edge of your image. This is caused from the sensor heating up from being on for so long, it creates little hot spots. It happens with really long exposures. Hope this helps.Joe', '2008-06-11 01:36:48.000000', '2008-06-11 01:37:18.000000', 0),
