(4763560, 684408, 72929, '<td valign="top">Argh! Had I known about this challenge I would''ve entered!! I was at a star party at a dark sky site on May 31st!!! Ugh!!<br/> <br/>Great shot of M16... and thanks to the advanced rules you could stack too! I like the diffraction spikes :)<br/> <br/>Have you heard about cloudynights.com? There is a DSLR imaging forum that is quite active. I am a participant there (by my full name) as well. You would be welcome to post there, plus you might pick up a few tips.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-11 09:13:13.</i></td>', 'Argh! Had I known about this challenge I would''ve entered!! I was at a star party at a dark sky site on May 31st!!! Ugh!! Great shot of M16... and thanks to the advanced rules you could stack too! I like the diffraction spikes :) Have you heard about cloudynights.com? There is a DSLR imaging forum that is quite active. I am a participant there (by my full name) as well. You would be welcome to post there, plus you might pick up a few tips.', '2008-06-11 10:12:36.000000', '2008-06-11 10:13:13.000000', 0),
(4763566, 685459, 72929, '<td valign="top">Kewl. Did you use a barndoor? I had the pleasure of taking the stargazing tour on Mauna Kea... wow, talk about dark skies. 10,000 feet altitude helps too.</td>', 'Kewl. Did you use a barndoor? I had the pleasure of taking the stargazing tour on Mauna Kea... wow, talk about dark skies. 10,000 feet altitude helps too.', '2008-06-11 10:16:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4763567, 684061, 72929, '<td valign="top">Argh! Had I known about this challenge I would''ve entered!! I was at a star party at a dark sky site on May 31st!!! Ugh!!<br/> <br/>Great shot of the milkyway, and thanks to the advanced editing rules you could stack too!<br/> <br/>Have you heard about cloudynights.com? There is a DSLR imaging forum that is quite active. I am a participant there (by my full name) as well. You would be welcome to post there, plus you might pick up a few tips.</td>', 'Argh! Had I known about this challenge I would''ve entered!! I was at a star party at a dark sky site on May 31st!!! Ugh!! Great shot of the milkyway, and thanks to the advanced editing rules you could stack too! Have you heard about cloudynights.com? There is a DSLR imaging forum that is quite active. I am a participant there (by my full name) as well. You would be welcome to post there, plus you might pick up a few tips.', '2008-06-11 10:17:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4763584, 685310, 72068, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by smurfguy:</b></div><hr/><i> For the picture itself, it''s an ok sunset.  A wider angle lens may have made it more interesting for me.  But for this challenge - no planets, moons, or stars. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>^ See description.</td>', 'Originally posted by smurfguy: For the picture itself, it''s an ok sunset.  A wider angle lens may have made it more interesting for me.  But for this challenge - no planets, moons, or stars.   ^ See description.', '2008-06-11 10:24:39.000000', NULL, 0),
